 - **Speed G2-CO, partial (built 2026-11-15, landed 2026-11-15; the concert at 30 on the GBA, speed audit 3 package S3-9 with the owner's 2026-11-13 trades and the choir experiment; measured on libmgba, PCSX-Redux and Flycast; docs/GBA.md "G2-CO: the concert at 30", ledger row G2-CO, docs/PS1.md "The concert (SP6, P-K1)"):** exact: the stage's still parts baked into the ROM for 31 keys (the Dreamland's with its clouds drawn live) and put back with one DMA (`DOOMO_BACKDROP_CONCERT`, `stage_parts`; kept == whole over 2,304 frames and every cloud position), a catch-up tick skips the stage, `look_run_hash` skips the resolve for an id with no run, Start keeps the song the setup made (every port; the Start frame 437 -> 105 ms), nothing drawn behind a closed curtain. Pixel-changing, GBA only (the GBA concert looks a little simpler than the PS1's): the setup screen held under its menu (S2-1's hold; the menu rows one pixel further in on the GBA), the closed curtain held while the show's pictures are drawn ahead, the flame wall in 6 wider flames of 4-row bars, the LED wall, lamps, beams, theme props and the Dreamland's clouds at 15 Hz (`plat_keep_rows`: the rows down to the wall's foot kept in the OBJ VRAM; `plat_beam_rows`; the grid and bats shows too), choirs above 12 voices at 85 % of their size. GBA drawn fps (`concert_profile.txt`): solo 21.9 -> **30.1**, choir 12 voices 14.5 -> **29.9** (full size), 16 voices 14.1 -> **29.9** (85 %), setup 14.3 -> **30.0**, the closed curtain 15.0 -> **30**, all with no frame over 33 ms; band 12.6 -> 20.5 with logic 22.5 -> 30.0. The choir experiment (singers at 100 / 85 / 75 / 66 / 50 %, 12 and 16 voices, with and without the trades): the scaling alone saves 2.5-3.1 ms at half size (12 voices 40.9 -> 38.4 ms, 20.3 -> 21.7 fps); with the flame and 15 Hz trades the full size holds 30 up to 12 voices and 85 % above. Tests: `concert_kept_stage_equals_the_full_stage`, `concert_dreamland_clouds_over_the_kept_stage`, `concert_stage_keys_cover