+### Speed wave 3: S3-7, the cutscene backdrops (SPEED-2 round 1, built 2026-11-15)
+
+Speed audit 3 package S3-7 (`core/src/cutscene.c`, `backdrop.c`; speed2 group `cutscene`, `gba/harness/scripts/speed2_cutscene.txt`).
+The story's vignettes drew their whole sky, wall, ground or room again on every tick, and every puff cloud as 20 circles (a
+circle is a rect call per row): the chapter-card-2 clouds 8 ms each, the fog's seven puffs plus the wall 94 ms. The audit only
+measured the first shot of each vignette; the later shots are worse (eruption shot 4: 161 ms of work, 6 fps).
+
+**What changed (the mechanisms; the Fun Fair's kept pictures of S2-4b, reused).**
+
+* **A kept still** (`cs_keep`, `cs_keep_rows`; backdrop family 4, `DOOMO_BACKDROP_CUTSCENE`): the home's room (wallpaper, floor,
+  window, bed), the fog's sky + Wall + Hillvile Lane's ground, the eruption's sky, Vapula's sky + spire (+ the plush on the
+  third shot) are pictures baked by the native runner with the scene's own drawing code (`bk_draw` calls the same `still_*`
+  functions the live path calls) and put back with one DMA copy (~3.2 ms a screen). Where nothing is kept (PS1, Dreamcast,
+  native, `hold` frames, 320x240) `cs_keep` says 0 and the scene draws the same thing itself, in its old order.
+* **A kept band**: the eruption's Wall and the ground in front of it (rows from the Wall's top to the bottom: 2 pictures) are put
+  back over the cloud; Vapula's shots 1 and 2 keep the sky, spire, shadow and the *demon* (the scaled sprite, `vid_blitn_arm`,
+  10 ms) as one picture per pose: 5 shudders of the wheeze, 5 sizes of the deflating Duke.
+* **Puff stamps** (`puff_cloud`; family 5, `DOOMO_BACKDROP_CUTSCENE_PUFF`): a cloud is a pure function of (radius, shade, the
+  breath `ui_wave(t, 48, 1)` in -1..1), so each wanted one is a stamp, one image blit (`plat_stage_stamp`): the fog's, card
+  2's and Vapula's clouds, and the eruption's up to a radius of 50 (`PUFF_STAMP_MAX`: a bigger one does not fit the screen
+  centred, and the baker refuses a stamp that touches an edge). `puff_wanted` lists the (ramp, shade, radius) the vignettes ask
+  for; it is also the key list, so the baked set and the asked set cannot drift apart (`cutscene_pictures_asked_for_are_baked`).
+* **The swelling cloud as a kept picture** (family 4, `CK_ERUPT_CLOUD`): from the second shot on the eruption's cloud is
+  50-114 px of radius, three puffs of 20 circles of up to 100 px (60-150 ms). The rows above the Wall (sky, the cloud, its two
+  side puffs, the grin) are one picture per size (82 of them: shots 2-4, one size every 2 ticks for 60 ticks), 80 rows each.
+* **Crowd bodies over ticks** (GBA only): `cs_draw` sets `bodyspr_lazy(3)`, the credits parade's mode, so a body the cache
+  lacks (~25 ms each; six at a shot's first tick) is drawn over the next ticks instead of in one 100-170 ms frame.
+
+**Same pixels.** `test_cutbk` plays the home, fog, eruption, Vapula and card 2 with the native stage on (its two emulated Mode 4
+pages) and off, 450-600 frames each, with A pressed to reach every shot: every frame is identical, at 240x160 and at 320x240 (fog,
+eruption), but for the three listed below. The baked key lists cover every picture the scenes ask for, and the baker refuses a
+stamp that touches a screen edge (`stage_bake_file_has_bands_and_stamps` runs every family). On the ROM, `vhash-seq` (`sync on 61`,
+base ROM `fe41002` against this one, the frames written out with `HARNESS_VHASH_SHOTS=1` and compared pixel by pixel): card 2 (200 frames) and the home
+(280) have the same sequence digests; fog, eruption shot 1 and Vapula's three shots equal the base outside the player's figure
+(its idle animation follows the draw speed: 100 ms frames in the base) and, on the crowd's shot, outside the crowd and the sky's
+seam row; eruption shots 2-4 differ only above the Wall (the cloud, below).
+
+**Pixel-changing (GBA only; before / after shots in the evidence directory).**
+1. The sky's *seam row* (row 53, `sky_bands`: half of it is painted by a checker and the other half was left to whatever the page
+   held, the picture of the scene before it): in the kept sky of the eruption and Vapula it is the dither the seam is meant to
+   be (the top colour under the middle colour's checker). The live path, the PS1 and the Dreamcast keep the old row (the test
+   does not compare it).
+2. The eruption's cloud past a radius of 50 (from the second shot on) does not breathe: the kept picture is drawn with a breath
+   of 0. The old cloud moved its odd lobes one pixel up and down; the difference is a one-pixel outline shift (see
+   `erudiff_*.png`). Smallest trade first: the cloud was exact up to 50 and the sizes beyond are 1.6 MB of ROM a breath
+   state would multiply by about ten.
+3. A crowd body the cache lacks shows a few ticks late (the credits parade's rule) instead of freezing one frame for 100-170 ms.
+
+**Results** (`make -C gba test-speed2 SPEED2=cutscene SPEED2_GATES=1`, windows of 90 ticks; drawn fps (work avg ms); the shot
+n windows follow the first by an A press):
+
+| window | before | after |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| chapter card 2 | 15.0 (59.6) | **30.0** (20.8) |
+| home, shot 1 / shot 2 | 24.0 (37.6) / 22.0 (38.3) | **30.0** (18.3) / **30.0** (19.0) |
+| fog, shot 1 / 2 / 3 (logic 18.4 / 16.9 / 18.4) | 10.0 (94.4) / 9.4 (103.2) / 10.0 (94.9) | **30.0** (27.7) / **30.0** (28.5) / **30.0** (28.1), logic 30 |
+| eruption, shot 1 / 2 / 3 / 4 | 16.8 (55.8) / 9.0 (108.7) / 7.1 (137.1) / 6.0 (161.0) | **30.0** (26.7) / **30.2** (14.9, one 50 ms frame) / **30.2** (19.1) / **30.0** (20.6) |
+| Vapula, shot 1 / after a press / shot 3 | 16.0 (57.7) / 20.0 (45.0) / 25.7 (36.4, 5 frames over 33 ms) | **30.0** (25.9) / **30.0** (18.5) / **29.8** (28.8, one 50 ms frame) |
+| chapter card 3, P0 bridge | 29.8 (17.4), 30.0 (27.5) | unchanged (29.8 (17.3), 29.8-30.0 (27.6-28.1): the audit's 40.3 ms bridge was fixed by S2-5 and S2-6) |
